 evidence from our notes. Our notes include many facts. We need to decide our provisional vote. We can either agree with Agent 3's recommendation of Candidate B, or propose another candidate based on evidence.\n\nLet's examine the facts:\n\nCandidate A: can anticipate dangerous situations (good), sees complex connections (good), excellent spatial vision (good), very good leadership qualities (good). Negatives: sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized.\n\nCandidate B: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress very well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather conditions (technical), excellent computer skills (technical). Negatives: can be grumpy, can be uncooperative.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly (decision quality), difficulty communicating ideas (communication), regarded as egocentric (cooperation), not very willing to further his education (adaptability), known to be 100% reliable (reliability), creates a positive atmosphere with his crew (cooperation). So C has reliability, positive crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately (stress resilience), can concentrate very well (attention), solves problems extremely well (technical), takes responsibility seriously (responsibility). Negatives: regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership skills.\n\nWe need to consider all criteria. Which candidate is best overall? Let's weigh.\n\nReliability: B (very conscientious), C (100% reliable). A unknown reliability, D unknown.\n\nStress resilience: B handles stress well, D responds adequately, A unknown, C unknown.\n\nTechnical competence: A sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision; B good at weather, computer skills; C quick decisions; D solves problems extremely well, concentration.\n\nDecision quality: C quick correct decisions; A anticipates dangerous situations; D adequate.\n\nAttention: D concentration; A unknown; B unknown; C unknown.\n\nCrew cooperation: A leadership qualities but sometimes not good at criticism; B can be uncooperative; C creates positive atmosphere but egocentric and communication difficulty; D arrogant, weak leadership.\n\nProfessional communication: B can be grumpy/uncooperative; A sometimes not good at taking criticism; C difficulty communicating ideas; D arrogant.\n\nResponsibility: D takes responsibility seriously; A leadership; B unknown; C positive atmosphere.\n\nOverall, B seems strong on reliability and stress, but has cooperation issues (uncooperative, grumpy). C is reliable, good crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric. D strong technical, responsibility, but arrogance and weak leadership. A strong technical and leadership but unorganized and not good at criticism.\n\nWhich candidate best fits overall? Might be Candidate C because reliability 100%, positive crew atmosphere, quick correct decisions, but communication difficulty could be mitigated. However egocentric and not willing to further education are concerns.\n\nCandidate B's uncooperative could be serious for crew. Candidate D's arrogance and weak leadership also serious.\n\nCandidate A's unorganized and not good at criticism could affect reliability.\n\nThus maybe C is best overall? Let's compare B vs C. B: reliability, stress, technical, but uncooperative. C: reliability, decision quality, positive crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric. Which is more severe? Uncooperative may affect safety more than communication difficulty? Both matter. Egocentric may affect teamwork. Positive atmosphere suggests good cooperation despite egocentric? Hard.\n\nWe need to make an argument. Could ask other panel members for more info on candidate B's uncooperativeness severity, or candidate C's communication difficulty. But we can also make a contribution now.\n\nWe should reference Agent 3's recommendation of B and either support or challenge. Let's challenge, propose C as stronger due to 100% reliability and positive crew atmosphere, and quick correct decisions, which are critical for long-distance flights. Acknowledge B's strengths but argue that uncooperative behavior is a bigger risk than C's communication difficulty, which can be trained.\n\nThus we vote for Candidate C.\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: C known to be 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere with crew, can make correct decisions quickly. Also note C difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nExplain why C is better overall.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate C\"."}
